course: dictionary
lesson: 15015
title: Resolved: solved or decided
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resolved has two main meanings. The first is solved or settled: when a problem is resolved, it is over. «The argument between Sam and Priya was resolved after they talked it through.» The clue is the talking: they fixed the argument.
explain: The second meaning is decided firmly. When you resolve to do something, you make up your mind to do it. «She resolved to practise the piano every day.» The clue is to do, which tells you she made a plan.
explain: Resolved can also describe a person who is determined. «I am resolved to finish this book before Friday» means I have made a firm decision and I will not give up. To check, swap in a word like settled or decided and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Resolved means solved or settled, as in «The problem was resolved».
fact: Resolved also means decided firmly, as in «She resolved to work harder».
fact: «Resolve to» is often followed by a verb: «He resolved to be kinder».
fact: New Year's resolutions are things people decide to do in the new year.
fact: Resolved as an adjective means determined, as in «I am resolved to win».
exercise: «The argument between Sam and Priya was resolved after they talked it through.» What does resolved mean here? | Shouted about loudly | Made much worse | Put off until next week | *Solved or settled
exercise: «She resolved to practise the piano every day.» What does resolved mean here? | *Decided firmly | Tried once and gave up | Forgot all about | Shouted loudly
exercise: «The maths puzzle took ages, but at last it was resolved.» In this sentence, what happened to the puzzle? | Lost | Started again | Hidden | *Solved
test: Jack resolved to read every night. What does resolved mean? | *Decided firmly to do something | Finished reading | Forgotten | Argued about
test: «The issue was resolved.» Which phrase means the same? | Was lost | Was made bigger | Was hidden away | *Was settled
exam: «The matter has been resolved» means what? | The matter has been argued about all day | The matter has been written down for later | The matter has been hidden from everyone | *The problem has been settled, so there is no longer an issue
